<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greenville, Liberia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Greenville is a port town on the coast of south-eastern Liberia and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinoe-county">Sinoe County</a>, at the mouth of the Sinoe river. It was founded in the late 1830s as the first town of Mississippi-in-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, a settlement of formerly enslaved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-americans">African Americans</a> organised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> Colonization Society, which joined Liberia in 1842. It has long been an outlet for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> and other produce of the interior.</p></div>
